        "finding": "Integrity check confirmed FEATURE_return_rate and FEATURE_return_line_count are exactly zero for all observations. Raw data analysis reveals that in the Online Retail II dataset, negative quantity transactions with Customer IDs ALWAYS have a 'C' prefix (cancellations). Transactions with negative quantities but no 'C' prefix (returns) only exist for guests (null Customer ID). Since temporal features only include identified customers, 'return' type transactions are naturally zero, and all refund behavior is captured in 'cancellation_line_count' and 'total_return_amount'. This is not a bug, but a semantic artifact of the raw data."
